    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=3c4d4b7b-1f58-8bea-9fd3-8ca0e41684ff": {
      "title": "Title IX Specialist",
      "description": "Title IX Specialist at Illinois Institute of Technology Skip to jobs Back to Job Openings Title IX Specialist Department Office of the President Job Location Chicago, IL Date Posted Posted 1 month ago Apply Share Link copied Title IX Specialist Compensation: $48,000 - $50,000, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Position Type/Schedule: This is a Full-Time, exempt position, Monday through Friday, 8:30 a.m. to 5:00 p.m. Work Location: Illinois Tech, 10 West 35th Street, Chicago, IL 60616. Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States, both presently and for the duration of employment with the university General Description The Title IX Specialist is responsible for helping to support the university’s compliance with the requirements set forth by the Title IX Educational Amendments Act, the Clery Act, the Violence Against Women Act (VAWA), and the Illinois Preventing Sexual Violence in Higher Education Act. The Title IX Specialist will report to the Title IX Coordinator and carry out the following responsibilities: remain informed of all changes/updated in guidance/law at the federal and state levels to implement an timely Title IX program to the campus community; manage Title IX investigations; manage informal resolution processes; manage intake reports and provide supportive measures; maintain impeccable internal records of reports received, investigations conducted, and informal resolutions undertaken in both Maxient and Microsoft 360 OneDrive. The Title IX Specialist will also manage the annual online faculty and staff sexual harassment prevention training; conduct educational training workshops with students and employees across the university; assist with the editing of the handbooks and marketing materials; collaborate annually with stakeholders across the campus to develop and implement Title IX marketing campaigns; assist with the completion of the annual Clery, ISPHVE, and state mandated sexual misconduct student survey reports. Manage all activities/reports in the Maxient and Microsoft 365. Communications This position requires a person with strong communication skills to communicate clearly verbally and in writing, using effective interpersonal skills to understand complicated Title IX policies and regulations. The person will work directly with the Title IX Coordinator to interpret policy and draft internal and external documents and marketing material. This person will possess active listening skills and accurate note-taking ability as well as strong editing skills for use when editing office resources documents, policy manuals, marketing material, and letter-writing campaigns to make the language clear, accurate, and student-friendly whenever possible. Customer Service This position requires effective interpersonal skills, including the ability to demonstrate empathy and use a trauma-informed approach when addressing sexual misconduct. It also requires someone who possesses the ability to engage and build trust with students, campus partners, and community organizations on an ongoing basis, making sure to use language that encourages collaboration. Key Responsibilities - Develop, coordinate, deliver, document, and manage annual campus wide and targeted Title IX training for students and employees, ensuring compliance with applicable state and federal laws. Use varied training methods and maintain open communication with campus partners, participants, and volunteer investigators. - Lead Title IX events, campaigns, and presentations throughout the year, including Sexual Assault Awareness Month and Domestic Violence Awareness Month. Seek opportunities to collaborate annually with campus stakeholders in developing these programs. - Conduct and manage informal resolutions for eligible Title IX reports, meeting with both parties and assisting them in reaching mutually agreed resolutions. - Conduct and manage Title IX investigations, including fact finding, interviews, review of inculpatory and exculpatory evidence, credibility assessments, case status updates, and report writing. Manage case records in Maxient and Microsoft 365. - Receive and process reports of Title IX sexual harassment and provide supportive measures to Illinois Tech community members. - Assist with updates to handbooks and marketing materials and support Public Safety and General Counsel in completing annual Clery and ISPHVE reports and state mandated sexual misconduct student survey reports. Stay informed of current Title IX law through webinars, local workshops, and ongoing training. Education & Experience - Bachelor’s degree in a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and relevant experience. - Some experience working in higher education or a field related to the position (sexual assault, domestic violence, law, etc.). - Some familiarity with Title IX law and the Illinois Preventing Sexual Violence in Higher Education Act. - Must have the ability to leverage technical resources and build their own technical abilities in the execution of work. - Working knowledge of local resources in the Chicagoland area available to support the campus community is preferred. Knowledge & Skills - Familiarity with Title IX regulations and applicable State of Illinois sexual harassment laws. - Some experience with investigations, complaint handling, and resolution processes is preferred. - Proficiency in Microsoft 365 applications. - General familiarity with Maxient and Banner systems is preferred. Supervision & Budget Authority This position does not currently have direct supervisory responsibilities or budgetary authority. Physical Environment and Requirements - Works primarily in a standard office setting, performing administrative, programmatic, and computer-based tasks for the majority of the workday. - May occasionally attend meetings, events, or perform work-related duties at other locations throughout the University campus, with or without reasonable accommodation. - May occasionally lift and transport materials, such as boxes, supplies, or event items, weighing up to 15 pounds, with or without reasonable accommodation. - Regularly performs repetitive motions, including typing and other computer-related tasks, throughout the workday. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary EEO Statement Illinois Institute of Technology is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, inclusion, and diversity. It is committed to fostering an inclusive environment and actively seeks applications from individuals of all backgrounds and identities, regardless of race, color, sex, marital status, religion, national origin, disability, age, unfavorable discharge from the military, status as a protected veteran, sexual orientation, including gender identity and expression, order of protection status, and/or genetic information. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology | Visit our home page Applicant tracking system powered by Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=19ee2990-a5f3-868d-5ca0-797b663d0cf5": {
      "title": "Assistant Director of Enrollment Marketing",
      "description": "Assistant Director of Enrollment Marketing at Illinois Institute of Technology Skip to jobs Back to Job Openings Assistant Director of Enrollment Marketing Department Marketing and Communications Job Location Chicago, IL Date Posted Posted 1 month ago Apply Share Link copied Assistant Director of Enrollment Marketing Position Details Compensation: $65,000–$75,000 yearly, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Position Type/Schedule: Full-time Work Location: Illinois Institute of Technology, Chicago, Illinois Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States, both presently and for the duration of employment with the university. Position Summary The Assistant Director of Enrollment Marketing supports the development, execution, and optimization of data-driven enrollment marketing strategies that advance undergraduate and graduate enrollment goals. This position manages recruitment communications, campaign execution, CRM-based marketing initiatives, analytics reporting, and project management while collaborating closely with Enrollment Management, Marketing and Communications, campus partners, and external vendors. The Assistant Director plays an important role in developing and executing prospective student communication strategies across multiple channels and uses data and analytics to evaluate campaign effectiveness, improve engagement, and support the university's enrollment objectives. Essential Duties and Responsibilities Execute integrated enrollment marketing campaigns across email, web, digital advertising, social media, print, and SMS channels. Manage prospective student communication plans and recruitment journeys within CRM platforms such as Slate. Collaborate with Enrollment Management teams to support recruitment events, campus visits, counselor engagement, application campaigns, and other enrollment initiatives. Develop, schedule, and deploy enrollment communications while ensuring consistency with university brand standards and applicable accessibility requirements. Monitor campaign performance and prepare regular reports on key performance indicators, including inquiry generation, conversion rates, engagement metrics, and enrollment outcomes. Assist with lead-generation initiatives, list acquisitions, and partnerships with college search and planning organizations. Coordinate content development with Marketing and Communications, including landing pages, emails, digital advertisements, video, print collateral, and other recruitment materials. Manage project timelines, workflows, vendor relationships, and deliverables to ensure projects are completed accurately and on schedule. Support enrollment marketing budget tracking and return-on-investment analysis. Train and support staff and campus partners on enrollment marketing tools, communications, processes, and best practices. Develop and maintain documentation of enrollment marketing processes, workflows, and standards. Perform other duties as assigned in support of Enrollment Management and university objectives. Qualifications Bachelor's degree required. Minimum of two years of relevant professional marketing experience. Experience developing or executing multi-channel marketing or communications campaigns. Experience working with digital communications, email marketing, web content, or related marketing platforms. Demonstrated ability to manage multiple projects, deadlines, and stakeholders simultaneously. Ability to analyze campaign data and translate results into actionable recommendations. Strong written, verbal, organizational, and interpersonal communication skills. Preferred Competencies Experience working in higher education, enrollment management, admissions, student recruitment, or a related environment. Experience using a CRM platform, preferably Slate. Knowledge of enrollment marketing strategies and prospective student communication journeys. Familiarity with email marketing, SMS communications, digital advertising, social media, and web-based recruitment strategies. Experience with marketing analytics, performance reporting, conversion tracking, and ROI analysis. Strong project management skills with the ability to coordinate projects involving multiple departments and external partners. Demonstrated attention to detail and commitment to maintaining brand consistency and accessibility standards. Ability to work collaboratively with diverse stakeholders and effectively train or support campus partners. Ability to use data to identify opportunities, evaluate effectiveness, and continuously improve enrollment marketing initiatives. Supervision & Budget Authority May supervise coordinators, student employees, interns, or external contractors and provide project leadership for enrollment marketing initiatives. Supports budget tracking, vendor management, and ROI analysis for enrollment marketing activities. Budget authority, if applicable, is exercised in accordance with university policies and departmental approval processes. Physical Qualifications The position primarily operates in a professional office environment and routinely requires the use of a computer and other standard office equipment. The employee must be able to communicate effectively with colleagues, students, prospective students, vendors, and other stakeholders and perform the essential functions of the position with or without reasonable accommodation. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary EEO Statement Illinois Institute of Technology is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, inclusion, and diversity. It is committed to fostering an inclusive environment and actively seeks applications from individuals of all backgrounds and identities, regardless of race, color, sex, marital status, religion, national origin, disability, age, unfavorable discharge from the military, status as a protected veteran, sexual orientation, including gender identity and expression, order of protection status, and/or genetic information. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology | Visit our home page Applicant tracking system powered by Powered by"
    },
