    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=e10788ff-dc5e-136a-f43b-089a593b78d7": {
      "title": "Arboretum Program Manager",
      "description": "Arboretum Program Manager at Illinois Institute of Technology Skip to jobs Back to Job Openings Arboretum Program Manager Department Main Campus Physical Operations Job Location Chicago, IL Date Posted Posted 3 months ago Apply Share Link copied Arboretum Program Manager Position Details Compensation: $90,000 - $95,000, commensurate with experience and qualifications. Position Type/Schedule: This is a full-time, exempt position with a regular Monday through Friday schedule. Occasional evening or weekend work may be required to support Arboretum programs, campus events, seasonal activities, or urgent tree and landscape needs. Work Location: Illinois Tech, 10 West 35 th Street, Chicago, IL 60616. Work Authorization: Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States, both presently and for the duration of employment with the university. Position Summary The Arboretum Program Manager provides leadership, stewardship, and program management for the Alphawood Arboretum at Illinois Institute of Technology: Illinois Tech, a certified Level I arboretum located on the University’s historic campus in Chicago’s Bronzeville neighborhood. The position is responsible for advancing and maintaining a high-quality and diverse portfolio of trees, prairie plantings, and other herbaceous landscapes in an urban educational environment. Key areas of responsibility include arboretum stewardship, tree care and maintenance, landscape planning, project management, campus and community programming, and collaboration with academic, community, and industry partners. The Arboretum Program Manager works to ensure a safe, welcoming, sustainable, and aesthetically engaging outdoor environment for students, faculty, staff, tenants, visitors, and the surrounding community. The position reports to the Associate Vice President for Facilities and collaborates with University departments and external partners in support of the Arboretum’s educational, environmental, and community objectives. Key Responsibilities & Accountabilities - Provide overall leadership and stewardship for the Alphawood Arboretum and support its continued development as a University and community resource. - Oversee tree care, condition assessment, maintenance, preservation, and safety activities for the University’s tree portfolio. - Develop and implement proactive tree and landscape management practices consistent with professional arboriculture, environmental, and safety standards. - Guide the continued expansion and diversification of the Arboretum’s tree and plant portfolio, including consideration of biodiversity, sustainability, campus history, landscape architecture, and long-term environmental conditions. - Grow the arboretum to reach Level II Accreditation. - Oversee the development and care of prairie plantings and other herbaceous landscapes associated with the Arboretum. - Plan and manage Arboretum and landscape projects, including project scope, vendor and contractor coordination, schedules, documentation, implementation, and preparation and coordination of materials supporting external funding opportunities for Arboretum programs and projects. - Maintain accurate tree, landscape, project, and program records using appropriate technology and information systems. - Develop educational programs, events, interpretive materials, tree walks, signage, and other resources that increase awareness and engagement with the Arboretum. - Collaborate with Faculty, students, and academic departments to support educational activities, experiential learning, and other academic initiatives that make appropriate use of the campus landscape and Arboretum resources. - Develop and maintain collaborative relationships with community organizations, public gardens, professional associations, industry partners, and subject matter experts. - Communicate Arboretum information, tree data, campus landscape information, and program activities to internal and external audiences. - Incorporate safety, environmental stewardship, sustainability, and applicable regulatory requirements into Arboretum activities and projects. - Perform other related duties as assigned. Required Qualifications - High school diploma or GED. - Arborist skill training. - Experience with tree care, arboriculture, landscape management, or a closely related area. - Ability to identify tree and plant species in the field. - Knowledge of tree care practices, including tree condition and safety, pruning, preservation, bracing, removal, soil conditions, fertilization, and disease and pest management. - Ability to read and interpret landscape plans and apply them to tree, plant, and outdoor projects. - Strong organizational, project management, problem-solving, and communication skills. - Ability to work independently while collaborating effectively with University colleagues, contractors, community partners, and subject matter experts. - ISA Certified Arborist credential or ability to obtain the credential within an established period following hire. - Valid driver’s license. Preferred Qualifications - Bachelor’s degree in Forestry, Arboriculture, Natural Resource Management, Horticulture, Landscape Management, or a related field. - Five or more years of related tree care, arboriculture, landscape, or program management experience. - Experience managing an arboretum, public garden, campus landscape, or similar outdoor environment. - Experience coordinating landscape or facilities projects involving contractors and external service providers. - Knowledge of geographic information systems, tree inventory or tracking systems, computer-aided design, or related technology. - Pesticide Commercial Applicator/Operator License. - Aerial lift, fall protection, forklift, or related safety certifications. Service Standards and Performance Expectations - Provides professional, responsive, and collaborative service to students, faculty, staff, tenants, visitors, community members, contractors, and external partners. - Proactively identifies tree, landscape, safety, maintenance, and program needs and coordinates appropriate solutions. - Maintains accurate and current records, project information, and program documentation. - Communicates clearly and effectively with internal and external stakeholders regarding Arboretum activities, projects, programs, and concerns. - Effectively manages multiple priorities, projects, and seasonal responsibilities while maintaining appropriate attention to safety, quality, and deadlines. - Builds and maintains productive relationships across the University and with community, industry, and professional partners. - Demonstrates sound judgment, accountability, environmental stewardship, and a commitment to maintaining a safe and welcoming campus environment. Supervision & Budget Authority - Provides supervision and work direction to assigned union, non-union, and student employees supporting Arboretum and landscape activities. - Coordinates work performed by contractors, vendors, and other service providers associated with Arboretum projects and operations. - Oversees the Arboretum program budget and related expenditures in accordance with University policies and established approval processes. Physical Qualifications - Work is performed in both office and outdoor environments. - Must be able to travel throughout campus and work outdoors in varying weather conditions. - Position may require bending, kneeling, climbing stairs or ladders, and accessing landscape and tree-care work areas. - May occasionally work at heights or around equipment used in tree and landscape maintenance. - Must be able to safely perform the physical activities necessary to inspect trees, landscapes, and project sites. - Reasonable accommodations may be made to enable qualified individuals with disabilities to perform the essential functions of the position, consistent with applicable law. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary EEO Statement Illinois Institute of Technology is an EEO/AA/Title VI/Title IX/Section 504/ADA/ADEA employer dedicated to building a community of excellence, equity, inclusion, and diversity. It is committed to fostering an inclusive environment and actively seeks applications from individuals of all backgrounds and identities, regardless of race, color, sex, marital status, religion, national origin, disability, age, unfavorable discharge from the military, status as a protected veteran, sexual orientation, including gender identity and expression, order of protection status, and/or genetic information. All qualified applicants will receive equal consideration for employment. © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology | Visit our home page Applicant tracking system powered by Powered by"
    },
    "https://www.iit.edu/hr/careers?jobId=443435d3-9dc7-b47a-cd82-e11bbfa0e7ae": {
      "title": "Men's Lacrosse Head coach",
      "description": "Men's Lacrosse Head coach at Illinois Institute of Technology Skip to jobs Back to Job Openings Men's Lacrosse Head coach Department Athletics Department Job Location Chicago, IL Date Posted Posted 3 months ago Apply Share Link copied The salary range for this role is $55,000-$60,000 and is commensurate with experience Successful candidate will be responsible for leadership, administration, and coaching of a college men’s Lacrosse team. Responsibilities will include recruiting quality student athletes, organizing and planning practices, implementing game strategies, scouting, coaching, scheduling, budgeting and planning team travel in compliance with university, the NAAC Conference, and NCAA rules and regulations. Strong recruiting, communication and organizational skills are all required and candidates must demonstrate a willingness to follow all policies in place by the university and athletic department. The position will have a second duty as assigned by the Director of athletics. The ideal candidate will have excellent verbal and written communication skills. Must project a positive professional image and be enthusiastically engaged in creating a positive experience for student-athletes. Experience recruiting highly academically qualified student athletes is a must. This position does not provide customer service to external customers and provides limited customer service to internal customers. Must be willing to work some nights and weekends Key Responsibilities Adhere to and enforce all policies and procedures of the University, Department of Athletics, as well as the rules and regulations of the NAAC Conference and NCAA. Recruit and retain highly qualified student athletes. Ensure compliance with NCAA guidelines for contacting and entertaining prospects. Work closely with admissions department to ensure selection of appropriate student athletes. Provide leadership and instruction in the personal and athletic development of student athletes, including counseling team members in academic, disciplinary and personal matters, when appropriate. Initiate and coordinate the selection, purchase, fitting and maintenance of team equipment, to include uniforms, athletic equipment and supplies. Schedule and conduct regular practice sessions as permitted by NCAA rules and regulations. Develop and implement strategies for motivating student athletes to perform at maximum levels as both individuals and a team. Arrange team travel, lodging and transportation arrangements within specified budget. Provide a complete travel itinerary to director of athletics prior to each overnight trip. Ensure that the team dresses appropriately when traveling. Assist with approved fundraising activities as requested. All team fundraising efforts must be approved by the Director of athletics after fund raising proposal form has been completed. Assist in attempts to increase interest in the sport and attendance at competitions. Work with The Director of Athletics in developing and articulating to student athletes the departmental and team rules regarding appearance, practice, class attendance, punctuality, dress code and general standards of behavior. Enforce policies and procedures outlined in student athlete handbook, team rules and apply appropriate disciplinary action. Ensure the safety of student athletes and coaching staff through careful monitoring of the condition of athletic equipment and facilities utilized by the designated sport. Submit requests for repair, maintenance and improvement of facilities to the Director for facilities and operations. Assure that sport camps related to the sport program adhere to all rules and regulations related to scheduling and NCAA procedures. Review and clearly understand all sections of department employee handbook. All department employees are accountable for following this document. Additional duties as assigned by the Director of Athletics. Supervises assistant coach(es) and one student employee. Maintain Budget Bachelors degree and two years of experience coaching Men's Lacrosse required. Preference will be given to applicants with experience at the NCAA Division III level. Preferred requirements master's degree, 3-5 years of experience of collegiate coaching experience preferred. The successful candidate will possess excellent interpersonal skills, and the ability to work independently with little direction or no supervision. Evening and weekend work is required. No additional licenses or certifications are required. May be required to stand for long periods and must be able to lift at least 25lbs. No exposure to unpleasant conditions. The position requires long periods of standing approximately 50% of the time as well as administration of office duties 50% of the time. Benefits Illinois Tech offers eligible employees a comprehensive benefits package that includes medical, dental, and vision coverage; life and long-term disability insurance; a 403(b) retirement plan with university contributions and matching for eligible employees; tuition assistance programs; flexible spending and commuter benefits; an employee assistance program; university holidays; and applicable paid and job-protected leave benefits. Eligibility, waiting periods, employee contributions, and coverage levels vary by benefit and position. Our commitment to employee well-being is reflected in our competitive benefits package located here: Benefits Summary © 2026 Illinois Institute of Technology | Visit our home page Applicant tracking system powered by Powered by"
    },
